.\" Distro-authored man page for the Fedora pidp8i package.
.\" Candidate for upstreaming to the PiDP-8/I project.
.TH CC8 1 "November 21, 2026" "PiDP-8/I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cc8 \- small C compiler targeting the PDP-8
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cc8
.RI [ \-tcsah ]
.RI [ \-dSYM [ =VALUE ]]
.RI [ \-l [ log ]]
.I files
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cc8
compiles a useful subset of C into PALGAIL assembly for the PDP-8,
following the model of the small compilers for 8-bit machines (the
usage line names the tool after its cross variant,
.IR sccXXXX ).
Its standard headers
.RI ( init.h ,
.IR libc.h )
install under
.IR /usr/share/pidp8i/include .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t
output the C source as assembler comments
.TP
.B \-a
do not put an argument count in the A to function calls
.TP
.BI \-d " SYM[=VALUE]"
define a macro
.TP
.B \-u
allow the undocumented 8085 instructions LDSI, LHLX and SHLX in the
cross-compilation path
.TP
.B \-s
assemble the generated output (not implemented)
.TP
.B \-c
link (not implemented)
.TP
.B \-h
show usage
.TP
.BI \-l [ log ]
write most or all messages to a log file
.PP
File arguments are the sources to compile; with no file names it reads
stdin and writes stdout.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR palbart (1),
.BR ptp2txt (1),
and
.I doc/cc8-manual.md
under
.IR /usr/share/doc/pidp8i/
